<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila willistoni subcellular Turing wavelength (1.5 µm, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 77.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 of slot 3211. Schnakenberg kinetics on a periodic 8.796 µm patch, calibrated so the fastest mode is the assigned 1.5 µm (1.466e-6 m) detail scale at geological age 0 Ma. Predecessor Drosophila virilis and successor Drosophila yakuba keep the same reaction terms and diffusivity ratio; absolute diffusivities follow body-length^0.35. The Hanson 2019 photograph is the specimen. Full credit for the sweep, ablation, segmentation, and goodness-of-fit waits on the measurements sidecar and the image-fitness test. Overall 77.1/100 (faithfulness 73.9, reproducibility 84.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 70, Morphometric validation 68, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_willistoni_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 1833875 B, 720×540 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 481ccd337d573ff3027fbb3cc9c1b91d39c61e61a01ed5031ce0d44d23ba727f (sha256 481ccd337d573ff3027fbb3cc9c1b91d39c61e61a01ed5031ce0d44d23ba727f), spec_fingerprint db43d14901fb6b4601bb2d4fcd69a0bd3c5388cab0d6eb64de70aadd7ba01054. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: db43d14901fb6b4601bb2d4fcd69a0bd3c5388cab0d6eb64de70aadd7ba01054; artifact_sha256: 481ccd337d573ff3027fbb3cc9c1b91d39c61e61a01ed5031ce0d44d23ba727f. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 gives the two-species kinetics used here. | Clark et al. 2007 describe the D. willistoni genome, sex-comb loss, and inversion polymorphism. | Jeong et al. 2008 describe abdominal pigmentation divergence in the yakuba/santomea pair. | Hanson 2019 is a CC BY-SA 4.0 photograph of an adult D. willistoni female.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.072, b=1.186, gamma=0.84, Du=0.015919 µm², Dv=0.214909 µm² are chosen so λ_max=1.466 µm. | Allometry λ ∝ L_body^0.35 and a cell diameter linear in body length are slot-specific reconstructions. | The periodic patch stands in for the repeating granule lattice inside an epidermal cell.; transfer_boundary: The photograph resolves the whole fly. The 1.5 µm field is painted onto the segmented abdomen; it is not a micrograph of granules.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Clark 2007 measured a 1.5 µm Turing wavelength. | Does not claim sex-comb loss is produced by this reaction-diffusion system. | Does not claim D. virilis is a literal ancestor or D. yakuba a literal descendant. | Does not reuse slot 2931 parameters (86 µm, alpha_scale 1.63, beta_offset 0.38).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.7]: Record Pearson r, RMSE, and KS for the wavelength law and the abdomen intensities.",
        "open need [parameter_sweep/model-fidelity, pressure P=1.5]: Fingerprint the equal-diffusivity ablation as a negative control.",
        "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=1.7]: Fingerprint the diffusivity-scale sweep and show that wavelength moves monotonically.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.9]: Record non-circular specimen segmentation metrics (coherency, foreground, KS) against the Hanson photograph.",
        "remediation needed: Fingerprint the diffusivity-scale sweep (Pearson r, RMSE, monotonicity) in the measurements sidecar.",
        "remediation needed: Fingerprint the equal-diffusivity ablation (negative control) beside the Turing field.",
        "remediation needed: Record goodness-of-fit (Pearson r > 0.98, RMSE, KS) and run the image-fitness test on the growth GIF.",
        "remediation needed: Record non-circular specimen CV metrics: abdomen mask, structure-tensor coherency, foreground fraction, and KS against the Hanson photograph." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.71e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

